                <pb facs="0998" n="905" sameAs="frus:frus1935v04/pg905"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.1928/448a Suppl.: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Panama</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Flexer</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-11-09T13:00:00-05:00">November 9, 1935—1
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>73. Department’s telegram No. 65, October 25, noon. Has the Legation been
                    approached by Panamanian authorities with a view to discussing the points listed
                    in the Department’s telegram referring to sales to ships? If so, please
                    telegraph substance of any such discussions and forward complete report by
                    airmail.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
